  "description": "This course covers robotics programming fundamentals including ROS (Robot Operating System) node communication, sensor data processing with OpenCV, motion control via PID algorithms, SLAM techniques using Gazebo and Rviz, and robotic arm programming with ROS MoveIt. Students will implement path planning algorithms like A* and RRT in simulation environments, interface with real hardware via serial communication, and develop autonomous navigation systems using ROS packages. Topics include robot kinematics, sensor fusion with Kalman filters, and real-time control systems using ROS 2. The course emphasizes practical implementation of robotics algorithms through hands-on lab projects.",
